# Build context exclusions.
#
# Without this file the context includes venv/ (multi-GB) and models/ (320 MB),
# both of which get uploaded to the daemon on every build for no reason.

# ── Virtual environments ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
venv/
.venv/
env/

# ── Generated models ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Excluded deliberately, for two reasons. It keeps 320 MB out of the context,
# and it stops the host's graphs from shadowing the ones the builder stage
# produces — the image must be built from export_onnx.py's output, not from
# whatever happens to be sitting in the working tree. models/ is gitignored, so
# a clean clone has nothing here anyway; excluding it means the local build and
# the clean-clone build take the same path.
models/

# ── Python ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# ── Caches ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.cache/
huggingface/

# ── VCS and tooling ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git/
.gitignore
.vscode/
.claude/
.report_build/
node_modules/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ── Local env and logs ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
*.log

# ── Not needed at build or runtime ───────────────────────────────────────────
# The benchmark and load-test scripts run from the host against the published
# port; they are not part of the served application.
benchmark_batch_sizes.py
benchmark_onnx.py
load_test.py
load_test_nocache.py
test_cache.py
test_requests.py
docker-compose.yml
Dockerfile
README.md
LICENSE
